public static int secondLargest(int[] arr) {
    if (arr == null || arr.length < 2) {
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("Array must have at least two elements");
    }

    int largest = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
    int secondLargest = Integer.MIN_VALUE;

    for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {

        if (arr[i] > largest) {
            secondLargest = largest;
            largest = arr[i];
        } 
        else if (arr[i] < largest && arr[i] > secondLargest) {
            secondLargest = arr[i];
        }
    }
    return secondLargest;
}
------------------------
Condition ka simple breakdown
1️⃣ if (arr[i] > largest)
New largest mil gaya
Purana largest → secondLargest
2️⃣ else if (arr[i] < largest && arr[i] > secondLargest)
Duplicate largest ignore
Proper second largest update
🗣️ Interview me kaise explain karogi?

“I maintain two variables, largest and secondLargest. While iterating, if the current element is greater than largest,
I shift largest to secondLargest. Otherwise, if it lies between largest and secondLargest, I update secondLargest. This works in O(n) time without sorting.”
